  facts:[
    {q:"Name three conditions supporting industrialization in Britain.",a:"Coal and iron, investment capital, agricultural changes, available labour, markets and transport connections were among the interacting conditions."},
    {q:"How did factory work differ from many household crafts?",a:"Factories concentrated machinery and workers, imposed schedules and divided production into specialised tasks."},
    {q:"Why did industrialization not automatically end slavery?",a:"Some industries relied on slave-produced raw materials; abolition required resistance, campaigning, law and political struggle."},
    {q:"How did Hobbes and Locke differ over government?",a:"Hobbes stressed strong sovereign authority for order; Locke stressed consent and protection of rights."},
    {q:"Which thinker is associated with separation of powers?",a:"Montesquieu."},
    {q:"What question should be asked when a historical document praises liberty?",a:"Who actually enjoyed that liberty, who was excluded and how the stated ideal was applied."}
  ],
